{%- comment -%}
  A limited edition (DESIGN.md §7.5, DS-05, DS-16): every image of the work whole on the mat;
  beside it the museum label from the product's artwork fields, medium, edition and size, the
  price, framing and one action. One template for every product: whether it's on sale yet comes
  from custom.coming_soon and custom.availability_note, and the framing choice from the linked
  frame (custom.featured_frame), so no product needs its own template (content model parts 3, 6).

  Framing (DS-137): a print with a linked frame offers Unframed or Framed in its one form, and
  Framed adds the frame nested under the print, so the cart, checkout and order show it as part of
  the work. The form posts both lines to /cart/add: the print, then the frame with the print as its
  parent and the choice as its quantity (0 or 1), so it works without JavaScript. A frame is sold
  only with its print: a frame's own page (product type Frame) points to its print instead.

  The archive note and framing text are the same on every product, so they're settings here.

  Beside the work sits only what it takes to decide and buy: label, price, framing, the action and
  the archive note. The description follows below at reading width, "About the work"
  (DESIGN.md §7.5), with any disclosures after it (DS-38).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant
  assign f = product.metafields.custom
  assign coming_soon = false
  if f.coming_soon.value == true
    assign coming_soon = true
  endif
  assign frame = f.featured_frame.value
  assign form_id = 'gs-product-' | append: section.id
  assign can_buy = true
  if coming_soon or product.available == false
    assign can_buy = false
  endif
  assign is_frame = false
  if product.type == 'Frame'
    assign is_frame = true
  endif
  # The framing choice shows when the print can be bought and its frame can too.
  assign framing = false
  if frame != blank and can_buy and frame.available
    assign framing = true
  endif
  # A limited edition has its label fields; a frame (or a product not yet migrated) doesn't, so it
  # gets no archive note and its text is headed Details.
  assign is_edition = false
  if f.artist.value != blank and f.artwork_title.value != blank
    assign is_edition = true
  endif
  # The images' alt when they have none of their own: the label in plain text ("Artist, Title,
  # year"), never the product title, whose italics are Unicode letters a screen reader spells out.
  # Each view is numbered when there is more than one.
  assign art_alt = product.title
  if is_edition
    assign art_alt = f.artist.value | append: ', ' | append: f.artwork_title.value
    if f.year.value != blank
      assign art_alt = art_alt | append: ', ' | append: f.year.value
    endif
  endif
  assign image_total = 0
  for media in product.media
    if media.media_type == 'image'
      assign image_total = image_total | plus: 1
    endif
  endfor
-%}
{%- comment -%}
  The first view, then the label, price and action, then the other views: below 990 px the action
  follows the work, however many views it has (DS-110). Each mat takes its view's shape (DS-111).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign image_number = 0
  assign lead_view = ''
  assign more_views = ''
-%}
{%- for media in product.media -%}
  {%- if media.media_type == 'image' -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign image_number = image_number | plus: 1
      assign this_alt = art_alt
      if image_total > 1
        assign view = 'products.view_of' | t: number: image_number, total: image_total
        assign this_alt = art_alt | append: '. ' | append: view
      endif
      assign art_ratio = media.preview_image.aspect_ratio
    -%}
    {%- if image_number == 1 -%}
      {%- capture lead_view -%}
        <div class="gs-artwork__lead"{% if art_ratio %} style="--gs-art-ratio: {{ art_ratio }}"{% endif %}>
          {%- render 'gs-media', image: media, preset: 'detail', priority: true, mode: 'artwork', shape: 'lg', alt: this_alt, title: product.title, enlarge: true -%}
        </div>
      {%- endcapture -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- capture more_views -%}
        {{- more_views -}}
        <li{% if art_ratio %} style="--gs-art-ratio: {{ art_ratio }}"{% endif %}>
          {%- render 'gs-media', image: media, preset: 'detail', mode: 'artwork', shape: 'lg', alt: this_alt, title: product.title, enlarge: true -%}
        </li>
      {%- endcapture -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- if is_frame -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    A frame on its own (DS-137): it's sold only with its print, so its page shows the print and
    sends people there, and to the gallery for a print they already own. The prints are those in
    Theme settings, All limited editions, whose linked frame is this one.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- capture frame_prints -%}
    {%- for item in settings.all_editions_collection.products -%}
      {%- if item.metafields.custom.featured_frame.value.id == product.id -%}
        <li>{%- render 'gs-artwork-tile', product: item, heading: 'h2', sizes: '(min-width: 1296px) 384px, (min-width: 750px) 31vw, 100vw' -%}</li>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  {%- endcapture -%}
  <div class="gs-container gs-lead-in">
    <header class="gs-page-head">
      {%- liquid
        assign title = 'products.frame_page.title' | t
        assign eyebrow = 'shop.crumb' | t
        assign deck = 'products.frame_page.deck' | t
        render 'gs-title-block', title: title, eyebrow: eyebrow, back: settings.shop_page, deck: deck
      -%}
      {%- if settings.contact_page != blank -%}
        <p>{{ 'products.frame_page.own_print_html' | t: url: settings.contact_page.url }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </header>
  </div>
  {%- if frame_prints != blank -%}
    <div class="gs-section gs-surface-paper">
      <div class="gs-container">
        <ul class="gs-grid gs-grid--artworks" role="list">{{- frame_prints -}}</ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- else -%}
<div class="gs-container--wide gs-container">
  <div class="gs-artwork{% if image_total == 0 %} gs-artwork--text{% endif %}"{% if image_total > 0 %} data-gs-lightbox{% endif %}>
    {%- comment -%} The larger view's caption, the museum label (DS-140). {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if image_total > 0 -%}
      <template data-gs-lightbox-caption>{%- render 'gs-artwork-label', product: product, class: 'gs-lightbox__label' -%}</template>
    {%- endif -%}
    {{- lead_view -}}

    <div class="gs-artwork__info">
      <div class="gs-artwork__head">
        {%- comment -%} A way back to the Shop, as the work page has to the collection, labelled as the menu names it (DS-102). {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if settings.shop_page != blank -%}
          <p class="gs-crumb"><a href="{{ settings.shop_page.url }}">{{ 'shop.crumb' | t }}</a></p>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- render 'gs-artwork-label', product: product, tag: 'h1', link: true -%}
        {%- if f.medium.value != blank or f.edition.value != blank or f.dimensions.value != blank -%}
          <div class="gs-artwork__facts">
            {%- if f.medium.value != blank -%}<p class="gs-meta">{{ f.medium.value | escape }}</p>{%- endif -%}
            {%- if f.edition.value != blank -%}<p class="gs-meta">{{ f.edition.value | escape }}</p>{%- endif -%}
            {%- if f.dimensions.value != blank -%}<p class="gs-meta">{{ f.dimensions.value | escape }}</p>{%- endif -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      <p class="gs-price">
        {%- if can_buy == false -%}
          {{- variant.price | money -}}
        {%- else -%}
          {%- render 'gs-price', product: product -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      </p>

      {%- form 'product', product, id: form_id, class: 'gs-form', data-gs-form: '' -%}
        {%- unless product.has_only_default_variant -%}
          {%- liquid
            # The select is named after the product's option, as the store calls it ("Colour"). A
            # product with more than one option gets the general word.
            assign option_label = 'products.option' | t
            if product.options.size == 1
              assign option_label = product.options.first
            endif
          -%}
          <div class="gs-field">
            <label class="gs-field__label" for="{{ form_id }}-variant">{{ option_label | escape }}</label>
            <span class="gs-select-wrap">
              <select class="gs-input gs-select" id="{{ form_id }}-variant" name="{% if framing %}items[0][id]{% else %}id{% endif %}">
                {%- for v in product.variants -%}
                  <option value="{{ v.id }}"{% if v.id == variant.id %} selected{% endif %}{% unless v.available %} disabled{% endunless %}>
                    {{- v.title | escape -}}{%- if product.price_varies -%}, {{ v.price | money }}{%- endif -%}
                    {%- unless v.available %} ({{ 'products.sold_out' | t }}){% endunless -%}
                  </option>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </select>
            </span>
          </div>
        {%- else -%}
          <input type="hidden" name="{% if framing %}items[0][id]{% else %}id{% endif %}" value="{{ variant.id }}">
        {%- endunless -%}

        {%- if framing -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            The choice is the frame's quantity: 0 adds the print alone, 1 adds the frame under it.
            With options, the parent follows the one chosen (gs-forms.js); without the script it
            stays off and the frame is added as its own line.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign frame_variant = frame.selected_or_first_available_variant
            assign frame_price = frame_variant.price | money
          -%}
          <input type="hidden" name="items[0][quantity]" value="1">
          <input type="hidden" name="items[1][id]" value="{{ frame_variant.id }}">
          {%- if product.has_only_default_variant -%}
            <input type="hidden" name="items[1][parent_id]" value="{{ variant.id }}">
          {%- else -%}
            <input type="hidden" name="items[1][parent_id]" value="{{ variant.id }}" disabled data-gs-parent-of="{{ form_id }}-variant">
          {%- endif -%}
          <fieldset class="gs-choice"{% if section.settings.framing_text != blank %} aria-describedby="{{ form_id }}-framing"{% endif %}>
            <legend class="gs-field__label">{{ 'products.framing' | t }}</legend>
            <label class="gs-choice__option"><input type="radio" name="items[1][quantity]" value="0" checked>{{ 'products.unframed' | t }}</label>
            <label class="gs-choice__option"><input type="radio" name="items[1][quantity]" value="1">{{ 'products.framed' | t: price: frame_price }}</label>
          </fieldset>
          {%- if section.settings.framing_text != blank -%}
            <div class="gs-prose gs-caption" id="{{ form_id }}-framing">{{ section.settings.framing_text }}</div>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%} Not on sale yet, or sold out: the reason sits beside the disabled button and describes it. {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if can_buy == false -%}
          <div class="gs-actions">
            <button class="gs-button" type="button" disabled aria-describedby="{{ form_id }}-why">{{ 'products.add_to_cart' | t }}</button>
            <p class="gs-note" id="{{ form_id }}-why">{%- render 'gs-price', product: product -%}</p>
          </div>
        {%- else -%}
          <button class="gs-button" type="submit" name="add" data-gs-busy-label="{{ 'products.adding' | t }}">{{ 'products.add_to_cart' | t }}</button>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endform -%}

      {%- liquid
        # The collection's copy of this edition (DS-181): the work whose In the Shop field names this
        # product, so the two pages link each other. Liquid can't find an entry by a field's value,
        # so it is looked for among the works of the edition's artists (its Artist pages field),
        # read inside a paginate tag: a plain loop stops at 50 (DS-152).
        assign collection_work_url = ''
        if is_edition
          for a in f.artist_entries.value
            paginate a.works.value by 250
              for w in a.works.value
                if w.in_the_shop.value.id == product.id
                  assign collection_work_url = w.system.url
                  break
                endif
              endfor
            endpaginate
            if collection_work_url != blank
              break
            endif
          endfor
        endif
      -%}
      {%- if is_edition and section.settings.archive_note != blank -%}
        <div class="gs-prose gs-caption">{%- render 'gs-linked-names', html: section.settings.archive_note, names_only: true -%}</div>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if collection_work_url != blank -%}
        <p><a class="gs-cta-link" href="{{ collection_work_url }}">{{ 'products.see_work' | t }}</a></p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        Without the choice: a print not on sale yet says framing will be offered; one on sale whose
        frame is sold out says so. A sold-out print says nothing about framing.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if frame != blank and framing == false -%}
        {%- if coming_soon and frame.available -%}
          {%- assign frame_price = frame.selected_or_first_available_variant.price | money -%}
          <p class="gs-meta">{{ 'products.framing_offered' | t: price: frame_price }}</p>
        {%- elsif can_buy -%}
          <p class="gs-meta">{{ 'products.framing_sold_out' | t }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}

    </div>

    {%- if more_views != blank -%}
      <ul class="gs-artwork__media">{{- more_views -}}</ul>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- liquid
      assign disclosures = product.metafields.shopify.disclosure.value
      assign has_disclosures = false
      for disclosure in disclosures
        if disclosure.display_preferences.value.surfaces contains 'product_page'
          assign has_disclosures = true
        endif
      endfor
    -%}
    {%- if product.description != blank or has_disclosures -%}
    <section class="gs-artwork__about" aria-labelledby="{{ form_id }}-about">
      <h2 class="gs-label" id="{{ form_id }}-about">{% if is_edition %}{{ 'products.about_work' | t }}{% else %}{{ 'products.details' | t }}{% endif %}</h2>
      {%- if product.description != blank -%}
        <div class="gs-prose">{%- capture html -%}{{ product.description }}{%- endcapture -%}{%- render 'gs-rich-text', html: html, link_names: true, names_only: true -%}</div>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- for disclosure in disclosures -%}
        {%- assign surfaces = disclosure.display_preferences.value.surfaces -%}
        {%- if surfaces contains 'product_page' -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign disclosure_title = disclosure.title.value
            if disclosure_title == blank
              assign disclosure_title = 'products.disclosure' | t
            endif
          -%}
          <details class="gs-disclosure">
            <summary>{{ disclosure_title | escape }}</summary>
            <div class="gs-disclosure__body gs-prose">{%- capture html -%}{{ disclosure.content | metafield_tag }}{%- endcapture -%}{%- render 'gs-rich-text', html: html -%}</div>
          </details>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </section>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Artwork",
  "tag": "section",
  "enabled_on": {
    "templates": ["product"]
  },
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The label comes from each product's artwork fields (artist, title, year, medium, edition, dimensions). Not yet on sale: turn on Coming soon and fill Availability note on the product."
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "archive_note",
      "label": "Note on every artwork",
      "default": "<p><em>The first edition is archived in the Artists For Kids and the Gordon Smith Gallery Permanent Collection</em></p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "framing_text",
      "label": "Framing text",
      "info": "Shown under the Framing choice when the product has a linked frame.",
      "default": "<p>Museum-quality framing and service includes UV-protective glass and acid-free matting, keeping your fine art print vibrant and pristine for decades.<br/>Framing by Artrageous Pictures and Framing North Shore</p>"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
